Z||000000||loafer87gt||03-20-2001||10:29 PM||||hmmm, seems like every vehicle I own has its quirks. For some reason the e-brake light keeps coming on in my 89 1/4 ton Toyota truck. It only does this under hard acceleration, and I can't figure out whats up. The previous owner of the truck installed a 3.4 Tacoma v6 in the truck, but I have driven the truck for nearly two years without any probs. Any ideas what the prob could be? Could it just be a sensor or something? I have checked the brake cables and they look OK, and NO the ebrake isn't on  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000001||fierospeeder||03-21-2001||12:00 AM||||i dont know anything about toyotas, does your have a brake fluid sensor?  If its not filled up all the way the light will go on.  My tbird has one of those and the light will go on under acceleration.||||reg||1
Z||000002||DJRice||03-21-2001||06:29 PM||||You might want to check your master cylinder to see if its full, but also check the hardware at all four wheels to see if you have a leak.  Typically, that light will come on to indicate a loss of pressure.<P>------------------<BR>Dillon<BR>Black '87 SE V6<P>"Who wants somma Debo?"||||reg||1
